WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.308
Home now shows you what to ride next, and opens both doors.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.759
It greets you by the time of day. The Next ride card offers the race that opens your

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:20.805
next map: top three on Old Town Criterium opens Neon Docklands, with your best

00:00:20.805 --> 00:00:21.493
there.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.428
A new rider is welcomed and sent to Prairie Paceline. A level goal counts the levels

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.657
still to climb.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.119
The Race door counts your maps and stars. An open tile goes straight to Race Setup;

00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:43.461
a locked one shows how to open it.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.399
The Classes door features 30 Minute HIIT Cardio, and Ride alone opens Class Start.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.386
When a ride opens a map, Home says so once, in gold, and the card has already moved

00:01:04.386 --> 00:01:04.868
on.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:15.628
From a phone to a laptop, Home lays itself out to fit.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.812
What the tests prove: the right map for every rider, both doors, and a banner that

00:01:29.812 --> 00:01:30.735
shows once.

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:40.097
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:40.443 --> 00:01:44.954
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:44.954 --> 00:01:46.625
every hill and interval.

00:01:46.971 --> 00:01:52.149
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:57.597
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:57.597 --> 00:02:00.587
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:00.932 --> 00:02:03.424
A custom workout lives under Profile.
